HST Office: the GTK file picker no longer crashes when windows open while it is up (Linux).

RunDialog queues an idle cancel (canceldialog) whenever another top window opens or the office is asked to
quit while the picker runs, and removed it in its destructor with g_source_remove_by_user_data(), which removes
only one of several sources with the same data. Two windows opening in a row while the picker was up (a
document loading, a start-up question) left a second cancel queued; it fired after the RunDialog was gone and
cast a freed dialog pointer: SIGSEGV in g_type_check_instance_cast from libvclplug_gtk3lo.so (canceldialog),
seen on Linux Mint 22.3 with 1.0.2. Now at most one cancel is queued per RunDialog, its source id is kept and
removed as soon as gtk_dialog_run returns and in the destructor, and a cancel only acts while the dialog runs.

